    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23177" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δᾴδουχ-ος</span></b> , ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>torch-bearer,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				2.17
			</span></i>: but usu. of the holder of a hereditary office at the
			mysteries of the Eleusinian Demeter, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				6.3.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1405a20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.76.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				2587.305
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. Κόρης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					3.172.9
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δᾳδοῦχοι τῆς σοφίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.10e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of the Sun,
				<i><span class="en">
				Cleanth.Stoic.
				1.123
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>torch-stand, candelabrum</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				4647
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Bostra</span>): also in 
				Lacon.
			 form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δᾳδῶχορ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
